<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15688" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">emplastrum</span></b> , i, n. (or
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">emplastra</span></b> , ae,
			f., <i><span class="en">Gell. 16, 7 <i>fin.</i></span></i>), =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔμπλαστρον</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In medic. lang., <i>a plaster.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> Prop., <i><span class="en">Cels. 5,
			17</span></i>; <i><span class="en">19</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 39, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 21, 4,
				10, § 15</span></i>; <i><span class="en">34, 10, 22, §
			103</span></i> et saep.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: quid est jusjurandum? Emplastrum
			aeris alieni, Laber. ap. <i><span class="en">Gell. 16, 7 <i>fin.</i></span></i> —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In horticult. lang., <i>the band of bark
				which surrounds the eye in ingrafting</i>, <i>the
				scutcheon</i>, <i><span class="en">Col. 5, 11, 10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id.
				Arb. 26, 9 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 17, 16, 26, § 121</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Pall. Febr. 17, 1 al.</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
